Creating bitmap fonts for GAL
=============================
Maciej Suminski <maciej.suminski@cern.ch>
12.04.2016

Adding a few glyphs
-------------------
To add individual glyphs the base font lacks (symbols, arrows) without
regenerating the whole atlas, run add_sdf_glyphs.py. It rasterizes the missing
glyphs from Noto, converts them to the atlas SDF encoding, and appends them in a
new shelf-band so the existing atlas stays byte-identical. Edit its SOURCES map
to choose codepoints, then update the pixels[] height it prints in
common/gal/opengl/gl_resources.h.

The house atlas (Monaspace Xenon)
---------------------------------
The house build (KICAD_HOUSE_FONTS) compiles common/gal/opengl/bitmap_font_xenon_img.c and
bitmap_font_xenon_desc.c instead of the Ubuntu Mono atlas, which every other build keeps unchanged.
make_house_atlas.py writes them from Monaspace Xenon Regular, keeping the upstream atlas's codepoints
and encoding: 48 texels per em, a 3-texel MSDF range, 1-texel borders, cells stored upside down.
Codepoints Xenon lacks keep the upstream glyph, centered in Xenon's 0.62 em advance.

The committed files were made with:
    msdf-atlas-gen v1.4 (github.com/Chlumsky/msdf-atlas-gen, MIT; tag v1.4, commit 2ede2543),
    built with -DMSDF_ATLAS_USE_VCPKG=OFF -DMSDF_ATLAS_USE_SKIA=OFF -DMSDFGEN_USE_VCPKG=OFF
    -DMSDFGEN_USE_SKIA=OFF -DMSDFGEN_DISABLE_SVG=ON -DMSDF_ATLAS_NO_ARTERY_FONT=ON
    MonaspaceXenon-Regular.otf from Monaspace 1.400 (github.com/githubnext/monaspace, OFL 1.1)

and this command, from the repository root:
    python3 tools/gal_bitmap_font/make_house_atlas.py \
        --font MonaspaceXenon-Regular.otf --msdf-atlas-gen msdf-atlas-gen

It prints the atlas height, which the house branch of pixels[] in common/gal/opengl/gl_resources.h
must match. With the same tool and font it reproduces the committed files byte for byte.

To create a new bitmap font atlas for Graphics Abstraction Layer, follow these steps:

 * Download Bitmap Font Generator [1] (runs well under wine)
 * Load default configuration stored in font.bmfc
 * Adjust settings as needed
 * Be sure that all glyphs fit into one page (you can check if in 'Visualize' you can move to another page (menu View))
 * Export font atlas as .PNG file, and font description as XML file
 * Run ./fnt2struct.py bitmap_font.fnt
 * Run ./png2struct.py bitmap_font_0.png
 * Copy bitmap_font_desc.c to common/gal/opengl/bitmap_font_desc.c
 * Copy bitmap_font_0.png to common/gal/opengl/bitmap_font_img.c

Recommended export options:
    Texture size: 1024x1024 or 2048x2048 (should be supported by majority GPUs)
    Bit depth: 8
    Font descriptor: XML
    Textures: png
    Layout spacing: 2 (both horizontal and vertical)

To match as closely as possible the newstroke_font glyph set,
mark the following character subsets in Bitmap Font Generator right panel:
    Latin + Latin Supplement
    Latin Extended A
    Latin Extended B
    IPA Extensions
    Greek and Coptic
    Cyrillic
    Latin Extended Additional
    Greek Extended
    General Punctuation
    Subscripts and Superscripts
    Currency Symbols
    Number Forms
    Mathematical Operators
    Geometric Shapes

References:
    1. http://www.angelcode.com/products/bmfont/
